From: PS4 port
Subject: [PATCH] orbis: give the path helpers a console arm

    deps/Framework/src/PathUtils.cpp:177: error: use of undeclared identifier 'getuid'

Same cause as swanstation's two patches: this SDK's libc++ undefines __FreeBSD__ on purpose, so a
C++ TU here has NO platform macro and falls through every #elif to the final #else - which builds
a home directory out of getpwuid(getuid()). getuid is declared in the SDK's unistd.h but the
overlay's shadows it, and neither libc.a nor libkernel.a defines it, so even declared it would
have been an undefined symbol at link.

⚠ ADDING __ORBIS__ TO THE LINUX/FreeBSD ARM WOULD COMPILE AND THEN CRASH. Every function in it is
`fs::path(getenv("HOME")) / something`, and this console has no HOME, no XDG_CONFIG_HOME and no
XDG_CACHE_HOME - so each one would construct fs::path from a null pointer. The arm needs real
paths, not a platform label.

/data/retroarch is where the frontend already keeps cores, system files, saves and playlists, so
Play!'s own data goes beside them rather than at a path nothing else on the console knows about.

diff --git a/deps/Framework/src/PathUtils.cpp b/deps/Framework/src/PathUtils.cpp
index f7a9f8b..0ec38d9 100644
--- a/deps/Framework/src/PathUtils.cpp
+++ b/deps/Framework/src/PathUtils.cpp
@@ -121,6 +121,33 @@ void PathUtils::SetCacheDirPath(const char* cacheDirPath)
 	s_cacheDirPath = cacheDirPath;
 }
 
+#elif defined(__ORBIS__)
+
+// This console has no HOME, no XDG_* and no passwd database, so every arm below would either
+// dereference a null getenv() or call getpwuid(getuid()) - which is what the #else arm does, and
+// what this file used to reach here. /data/retroarch is where the frontend keeps everything else.
+#define ORBIS_PLAY_DATA_PATH "/data/retroarch/system/play"
+
+fs::path PathUtils::GetAppResourcesPath()
+{
+	return ORBIS_PLAY_DATA_PATH;
+}
+
+fs::path PathUtils::GetRoamingDataPath()
+{
+	return ORBIS_PLAY_DATA_PATH;
+}
+
+fs::path PathUtils::GetPersonalDataPath()
+{
+	return ORBIS_PLAY_DATA_PATH;
+}
+
+fs::path PathUtils::GetCachePath()
+{
+	return fs::path(ORBIS_PLAY_DATA_PATH) / "cache";
+}
+
 #elif defined(__linux__) || defined(__FreeBSD__) || defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__)
 
 fs::path PathUtils::GetAppResourcesPath()
